  "statuteText": "79-A:11 Appeal to Superior Court. –\n\nIf the assessing officials deny in whole or in part any application for classification as open space land, or grant a different classification from that applied for, the applicant, having complied with the requirements of RSA 79-A:5, II may, within 6 months after notice of denial or classification, apply by petition to the superior court of the county, which shall make such order thereon as justice requires. Any appeal to the superior court under this section shall be in lieu of an appeal to the board of tax and land appeals pursuant to RSA 79-A:9."
